# Template Module Module

<!-- TODO(new-module): rewrite this page for the real module. The example lesson below must stay
complete and valid: authoringDocExamples.test.js parses and validates it. -->

A Template Module lesson (or a composed-lesson task with `moduleType: template_module`) is a
**workspace module**: students build up work that is saved on the device, carries through to
later tasks, and can be reset, revealed and shared by the teacher. The student writes in the
Template Module workspace and presses **Check**; the task's checks mark the work.

Write `type: template_module` on the lesson, or `moduleType: template_module` on a code task in a
`type: composed` lesson. In the Builder, create a **Template Module** lesson (or pick it in a
composed lesson's module picker).

## Complete example

```yaml
id: template-module-example
type: template_module
title: "Template Module example"
description: A short lesson using the Template Module workspace.
tasks:
  - title: Say hello
    description: Finish the sentence so it says hello, then press Check.
    starterCode: "say "
    completeCode: "say hello"
    check:
      type: code_contains
      value: hello
  - title: Say it again
    description: Your work from the last task carries through. Add a second hello.
    carryCodeFrom: 1
    check:
      type: code_contains
      value: hello hello
```

## Task fields

| Field | Required | Notes |
|---|:---:|---|
| `starterCode` | No | The work the task starts with. |
| `codeStages` | No | Starter / support / complete stages; each stage's work is in `code`. |
| `completeCode` | No | The finished work: shown by the teacher's **Complete** tab and offered to the student after two failed checks. |
| `carryCodeFrom` | No | A previous task's `id`: start from the student's saved work on that task. |
| `check` | No | One check or a list. Only code checks (`code`, `code_contains`, `code_equals`, …) are evaluated, against the work text, when the student presses **Check**. |

Lesson fields: `sandboxStarter` (text) turns on the personal sandbox after a passed task and is
the teacher's sandbox starter.

## Checks

| Type | Passes when |
|---|---|
| `code_contains` / `code_does_not_contain` | the work contains / does not contain `value` |
| `code_equals` / `code_not_equals` | the work is / is not exactly `value` |

## Teacher tools

- **Starter / stage / Complete tabs** show the task's authored work; **Send to all** pushes a stage.
- **Student card** and **watch** mirror the student's work (read-only).
- **Reset** (Starter / a stage / Complete) replaces a student's work.
- **Sandbox**: the teacher's shared sandbox is editable and can be pushed to the class.

## Validation

Messages specific to this module are listed under **Template Module** in
[validation-errors.md](validation-errors.md); the shared check messages apply too.
